==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Taitenki CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit may seem good at first; it has a high standing range, good LD pierce, low cost for an uber, surge immune, and strong vs. Alien and Aku. She does '''46,920''' damage with strengthen vs Aku at level 30 and '''56,304''' against Aliens. This can be amplified further if you boost her to level 40 or even 50, but that's likely not the best use of your Uber Catseyes.

She also is Immune to Surge, which is useful for her Aku matchup since annoying [[Surge Attack#Death Surge|Death Surges]] from enemies like [[Condemned Peng]] and [[Fallen Bear]] won't be able to take her out. Her long piercing range is also nice for Aliens, as the trait tends to have a lot of backliners, like [[Alpacky]], [[Calamary]], [[Elder Sloth]], and [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]]. Her 720 LD range can hit all of those enemies safely, as long as she has a stepping stone. All of this for only 3,600 cost seems quite handy...

But that is where her strengths end.

Firstly, her base HP is very low. She may have decent health against her traits, but she only has a measly 34,000 base HP at level 30, so using her outside of her niche is a death sentence. Backliners like Taitenki typically have a low HP stat to compensate for high damage or great Crowd-Control, but in this case, it does not balance out. Even if you perfectly protect her, she'll only deal '''23,460''' damage per hit to Aku, and '''28,152''' damage per hit to Alien, which is underwhelming considering her 6 second attack rate.

While this unit can deal high damage while strengthened, this unit's full potential is very reliant on that ability. In order for her to deal her full damage, she needs to take hits. This is obviously not good as letting the enemies push to your backline is a risky move that can result in a loss. Even as a failsafe, she won't survive long after taking hits. So even if you do manage to recover, she's already lost at least half of her HP,and half of her knockbacks, which means less chances to reposition. Repositioning is crucial for backliners like Taitenki to last in battle, losing half of those already low knockbacks means the next time the enemy frontline pushes, she's almost guaranteed to die.

Yet another flaw is her low proc rate. Taitenki has a 24% chance to pierce shields and break barriers.This may sound useful for her matchups against akus and starred aliens, until you realize just how rare it is for her to actually successfully proc. Her inconsistency as a piercer/breaker is amplified thanks to her extremely low proc chance (especially for an uber), and her sluggish attack rate. There are many better non-collab Shield Piercers like [[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Summoner Satoru]] or [[White Knight Cyclops (Uber Rare Cat)|White Knight Cyclops]], and even more no-gacha units like [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] and [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]]. And for barrier breakers, cats such as [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fencer Cat]] or any of the Elemental Pixies will do.

Finally, her blindspot. While it may not be as large as other units like [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Aphrodite]], those units can actually keep enemies away with their high attack damage. Taitenki has a blindspot of 320 range, which is large, yet small enough to where enemies can push slightly and damage her. This is likely why she has the strengthen ability. This is just a given for most LD ubers though, so nothing too special here.

Overall, Taitenki is a mid tier sniper Uber with low proc rates that gets outclassed in multiple scenarios, and has a weird strengthen that doesn't really work that well.

